p.src:
Take the two-photon decay channel in the positronium rest frame: $\mathrm{Ps}\longrightarrow\gamma+\gamma.$ Initially the total momentum is zero. Momentum conservation therefore requires the photons to emerge back to back with equal and opposite momenta: $\vec p_1=\vec p,
\qquad
\vec p_2=-\vec p.$ If $M$ is the positronium mass, energy conservation gives $Mc^2
=E_1+E_2
=c|\vec p_1|+c|\vec p_2|
=2c|\vec p|.$ Hence $\boxed{
|\vec p|=\frac{Mc}{2},
\qquad
E_1=E_2=\frac{Mc^2}{2}
}.$

